{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall place on the arrangement pure frankincense.</b> The bread of the Presence and the frankincense were mutually indispensable, like the etrog with the lulav, or like tekhelet with the white [linen] when tekhelet is available. And understand this: that is why you will not find frankincense in the meal-offering of the sotah, and likewise in the meal-offering of the sinner — as it is written (Numbers 5:15): ״לא יצוק עליו שמן ולא יתן עליו לבונה״ — because the attribute of judgment is drawn against them." "<b>And it shall be for the bread as a remembrance.</b> Because the bread of the Presence had no portion for Above but only the frankincense upon it — for in every arrangement they would offer the frankincense as incense — therefore the Torah says והיתה הלבונה ללחם לאזכרה, 'and the frankincense shall be for the bread as a remembrance,' for through the offering of the frankincense that is upon the bread, the bread is remembered on high and blessing rests upon it, and from it [comes] sustenance for the world. And from this you will understand what was the cause of the blessing in the bread of the Presence: all the sustenance in the world is blessed on its account. And understand this, for therefore there were twelve loaves arranged upon the table, and from there the blessing came, corresponding to the twelve angels that surround the throne of His glory; and they are called the four camps of the Shekhinah, for from there the world is blessed to its four winds, and they stand three to each direction, in the manner of the four standards of the desert. And corresponding to them in Solomon's throne were twelve lions. And in these twelve loaves there were twenty-four tenths, and you should be roused to this."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:03.636830188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}